  "worked_solution": "We divide both sides of the equation by $\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x$ and use the identity $\\operatorname{tan}\u2061x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x}{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x}.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x & =5\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x \\\\ \\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x}{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x} & =\\frac{5\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x}{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x} \\\\ 2\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x}{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x} & =5 \\\\ 2\\operatorname{tan}\u2061x & =5 \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}\u2061x & =\\frac{5}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\operatorname{arctan}\u2061(\\frac{5}{2})\u22481.190\\,29\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $5$ decimal places. \n\nTo find another solution in the interval $[-\\pi ,\\pi )$, we subtract $\\pi :$\n\n$$\nx\u22481.190\\,29-\\pi \u2248-1.951\\,30\n$$\n\nrounded to $5$ decimal places. \n\nSo, in ascending order, rounded to two decimal places, the solutions are \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}\u2248-1.95,\\,{x}_{2}\u22481.19.\n$$",
